> # llama-cpp-rdna-boosts A patch collection that brings **AMD RDNA-specific performance work** to [llama.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp): MTP decode, chunked gated-delta-net prefill, BF16 KV and WMMA flash-attention, fused MoE and k-quant decode paths, a hybrid all-reduce, qwen4exp (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) support, and an attention-memory campaign that frees several GiB of VRAM. It ships as **16 patches** (block 00 + blocks 01-15) for a clean llama.cpp checkout at the fork point **`790cf5 ... (truncated)
Based0.42.028.850 I sched_graph_realloc: graph reallocation: nodes = 5217 (changed = 0), splits = 50, n_same = 6, n_diff = 0
 on the detailed README and changelog you provided, here is a structured summary of the **llama-cpp-rdna-boosts** patch collection. This project is a specialized optimization suite for **llama.cpp** targeting **AMD RDNA** GPUs (specifically RDNA3, 3.5, and 4), delivering significant performance gains, memory savings, and new model support.

### 🚀 Core Value Proposition
This is a **16-patch collection** (Block 00 + Blocks 01–15)0.45.049.589 I slot print_timing: id  0 | task 0 | n_gen =    115, tg =  37.73 t/s, tg_3s =  38.06 t/s
